  "description_text": "A true Bellevue Hill standout, this striking Victorian Painted Lady makes an impression before you even step inside. Set on a coveted corner lot on Anawan Avenue, its sunny yellow exterior, intricate trim, and distinctive turret capture the grandeur of a bygone era. Beyond the ornate front door, a classic vestibule opens to a grand staircase and an expansive living space, where high ceilings, oversized windows, and room for two sitting areas create an inviting setting for everyday living and entertaining. A double-sided fireplace connects the living and dining rooms, bringing warmth and architectural interest to the open layout. The beautifully appointed kitchen features custom cabinetry, a farmhouse sink, generous island seating, and high-end appliances, including a double oven, gas cooktop, and drawer microwave, plus a dedicated coffee nook. The second floor offers four bedrooms, including a primary suite with custom closets and built-in wardrobes, and a beautifully finished bath with steam shower and heated towel rack. Three additional bedrooms share a full bath with skylight, while convenient in-unit laundry completes the floor. The third floor feels like a retreat of its own, with an additional primary suite and ensuite bath, a private sauna, and a separate office. Follow the spiral staircase into the turret for sweeping views of the Blue Hills and downtown Boston-a fitting vantage point for a home this distinctive. Outdoors, enjoy a rear deck, pergola-covered patio, and mature landscaping. With a bus stop at your doorstep, Bellevue Station less than half a mile away, and the shops, restaurants, and neighborhood amenities of Centre Street nearby, this remarkable home pairs architectural character and modern comfort with an enviable Bellevue Hill location.",
